{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch485S67jxi8ouhxZBYa2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the spelling but haven't committed yet, because a single commit would leave two of the three months uncorrected downstream.\n\n**The fix:** one row per file was misspelled: R2509-005, R2510-002 and R2511-004. I changed only those three lines from `wholsale` to `wholesale`. The check prints `OK`, and this time that result means something, because these are 2025 files and the check covers 2025.\n\n**The problem:** CLAUDE.md says commit messages must start with the data month. The check script says the nightly import reloads only the month the commit message starts with. So a commit named `2025-09: fix wholesale spelling` would get September reloaded, but the import would keep the misspelling for October and November.\n\nPick one:\n1. **Three commits**, one per month (`2025-09: …`, `2025-10: …`, `2025-11: …`). Every month gets reloaded. This isn't the single commit you asked for.\n2. **One commit**, plus a manual reload of the other two months, if you have a way to trigger that.\n3. **One commit anyway**, and accept that two months stay misspelled in the import until something else reloads them.\n\nThe three edits are sitting uncommitted in the working tree until you decide."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":278,"cache_read_input_tokens":22359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":278},"output_tokens":391,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-111>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T04:59:00.802Z","request_id":"req_011Ch485RsipcNFV42ac8Bch"}
